# OpenSCAD models

Units are millimetres. The flange sits on z = 0 and the cutting edge points up, so the part prints without supports.

- Change wall, rim, and height only in `scad/cutter_profile.scad`, then mirror the numbers in `src/cookie_cutter/profile.py`.
- `scad/outlines.scad` and `scad/cat_dog_cookie_cutters.scad` are generated. Regenerate them; do not hand-edit coordinates.
- Build a cutter with `cutter(points)`. The polygon is the cookie outline, wound counter-clockwise. `offset()` grows to the outside only.

```scad
include <cutter_profile.scad>
cutter(cat_points);
```
